Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Decree shall enter into force on April 18, 2019.
Article 2 (Transitional measures regarding subject matters of consultation on marine spatial compatibility)
In any of the following cases in connection with the approval, formulation, or modification of a use and development plan, or the designation of a district or zone, etc. or modification of such designation as at the time this Decree enters into force, the relevant use and development plan, as well as the relevant district or zone, etc. shall be excluded from consultation on marine spatial compatibility, notwithstanding Article 13 (2) and the Appendix:
1.Where consultation or evaluation specified in any of the subparagraphs of Article 13 (2) is requested;
2. Where consultation with the head of an administrative agency under the Appendix, submission of opinions, or deliberation by the deliberative committee is requested in accordance with the relevant statutes or regulations;
3. Where a request for approval, designation, etc. is made to the head of an administrative agency under the relevant statutes or regulations (applicable only to cases where the procedures under subparagraph 2 are not followed).

